content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "17902",
  "key": "SFCC-52",
  "summary": "Global Header UI",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Desktop/Mobile:*\n\n# Given a shopper visits any page on the storefront, when the page loads, then the global header is displayed at the top of the page on both desktop and mobile.\n# Given a shopper scrolls down the page, when the page is scrolled, then the top navigation remains sticky and visible at the top of the screen.\n# Given a shopper clicks the Zimmermann logo, when the click is registered, then the shopper is navigated to the homepage.\n# Given a shopper has items in their bag, when they view the header, then the Bag icon displays the correct running count of items.\n# Given a bag item is added or removed, when the bag is updated, then the Bag icon count updates without requiring a full page reload.\n\n*Desktop:*\n\n# Given a shopper views the header, when the page loads, then all header icons (Search, Account, Saved, Bag) are visible per the linked Figma Design.\n\n*Mobile:*\n\n# Given a shopper views the site on mobile, when any page loads, then the hamburger icon is displayed top-left in the header alongside Search and Bag icons top-right.\n# Given a shopper taps the hamburger icon, when the tap is registered, then the full-screen navigation drawer opens and the hamburger icon is replaced by a close (×) icon.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper taps the close (×) icon, then the drawer closes and the hamburger icon is restored.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper views it, then all top-level navigation categories are displayed vertically in the correct order per the linked Figma design.\n# Given the navigation drawer is open, when a shopper views it, then Saved and Account links are displayed below the main navigation categories."
  }
}"}

