content.content:
{"result":"{
  "id": "18141",
  "key": "SFCC-96",
  "summary": "Expanded Navigation - PWA Kit and Contentful",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "+*Content Type*+\n\n*AC1: Contentful content type*\n\n* Given the Contentful content type is created, when a Site Merchandiser opens the content model, then it includes nav item label, link/slug, item type (subcategory or editorial), display order, campaign image, and storefront scoping.\n\n*AC2: Contentful authoring*\n\n* Given a Site Merchandiser creates or updates a nav entry in Contentful and publishes it, when the page loads after publishing, then the updated links, ordering, or imagery are reflected across all breakpoints without a code deployment.\n\n+*Structure - Desktop*+\n\n*AC3: Mega menu trigger — desktop*\n\n* Given a shopper is on desktop and hovers over or clicks a top-level nav item that triggers a mega menu (NEW, CLOTHING, ACCESSORIES, COLLECTIONS), when the interaction occurs, then the mega menu panel renders below the navigation bar overlaying the page content.\n\n*AC4: Mega menu layout — desktop*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on desktop, when it renders, then it displays a left panel of sub-category text links and editorial links organised in rows and a right panel containing a full-height editorial image.\n\n*AC5: Collections two-column layout — desktop*\n\n* Given the Collections category is active on desktop, when the mega menu opens, then sub-category links in the left panel are displayed in two columns with group headings (READY TO WEAR, SWIM & RESORT).\n\n*AC6: Page overlay — desktop*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on desktop, when it renders, then a semi-transparent dark overlay is applied to the page content beneath the panel.\n\n*AC7: Active nav item underline — desktop*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open, when a top-level nav item is triggering the mega menu, then that nav item is displayed with an underline indicating it is active.\n\n+*Structure — Tablet*+\n\n*AC8: Mega menu trigger — tablet*\n\n* Given a shopper is on tablet and hovers over or clicks a top-level nav item that triggers a mega menu, when the interaction occurs, then the mega menu panel renders below the navigation bar overlaying the page content.\n\n*AC9: Mega menu layout — tablet*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on tablet, when it renders, then it displays sub-category text links and editorial on top, with a full width editorial image below.\n\n*AC10: Collections two-column layout — tablet* \n\n* Given the Collections category is active on tablet, when the mega menu opens, then sub-category links are displayed in two columns with group headings (READY TO WEAR, SWIM & RESORT).\n\n*AC11: Page overlay — tablet*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on tablet, when it renders, then a semi-transparent dark overlay is applied to the page content beneath the panel\n\n*AC12: Active nav item underline — tablet*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open, when a top-level nav item is triggering the mega menu, then that nav item is displayed with an underline indicating it is active.\n\n+*Structure — Mobile*+\n\n*AC13: Mobile menu trigger*\n\n* Given a shopper is on mobile and taps the hamburger icon (≡), when the interaction occurs, then the mobile menu drawer opens as a full-width overlay displaying all top-level nav items (NEW, CLOTHING, ACCESSORIES, COLLECTIONS, Z.IMMERSE) as large heading-level links.\n\n*AC14: Mobile menu — Wishlist and Account*\n\n* Given the mobile menu drawer is open, when it renders, then Wishlist (with dynamic item count if applicable) and Account links are displayed below the top-level nav items.\n\n*AC15: Mobile menu — close icon*\n\n* Given the mobile menu drawer is open, when the shopper taps the close icon (×), then the drawer dismisses and the hamburger icon (≡) is restored.\n\n*AC16: Mobile menu — no mega menu*\n\n* Given a shopper taps a top-level nav item on mobile, when the interaction occurs, then the shopper is navigated directly to the corresponding category PLP - no mega menu panel renders on mobile.\n\n+*Dismiss Behaviour*+\n\n*AC17: Mega menu stays open while cursor is within panel*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on desktop or tablet, when the shopper's cursor remains within either the triggering nav item or the mega menu panel, then the mega menu stays open.\n\n*AC18: Mega menu dismisses on cursor exit*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on desktop or tablet, when the shopper's cursor leaves both the triggering nav item and the mega menu panel boundary, then the mega menu dismisses.\n\n*AC19: Dismiss via CLOSE X*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open on desktop or tablet, when the shopper clicks CLOSE X in the nav bar, then the mega menu dismisses and the nav icons are restored.\n\n*AC20: Dismiss via Escape*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open, when the shopper presses Escape, then the mega menu dismisses and focus returns to the triggering nav item.\n\n*AC21: Dismiss on sub-category link click*\n\n* Given the mega menu is open, when the shopper clicks a sub-category link or editorial link, then they are navigated to the correct destination and the mega menu dismisses.\n\n*AC22: Z.IMMERSE — no mega menu*\n\n* Given a shopper hovers over or clicks Z.IMMERSE on desktop or tablet, when the interaction occurs, then no mega menu appears and the shopper is navigated directly to the Z.IMMERSE destination page.\n\n+*Sub-category & Editorial Links*+\n\n*AC23: Sub-category links driven by BM via Contentful category ID*\n\n* Given the mega menu renders for a nav item, when the left panel loads, then sub-category links are fetched from the SFCC category taxonomy via the BM catalogue using the category ID stored in Contentful and are not hardcoded in the component.\n\n*AC24: Editorial links driven by Contentful*\n\n* Given the mega menu renders for a nav item, when the left panel loads, then editorial links are fetched from Contentful for that nav item using the active storefront and are not hardcoded in the component.\n\n*AC25: Sub-category link navigation*\n\n* Given a sub-category link is clicked, when the shopper selects it, then they are navigated to the corresponding category PLP.\n\n*AC26: Editorial link navigation*\n\n* Given an editorial link is clicked, when the shopper selects it, then they are navigated to the corresponding destination page.\n\n*AC27: Offline sub-category hidden*\n\n* Given a sub-category is set to offline in Business Manager for the active storefront, when the mega menu renders, then the corresponding sub-category link does not appear.\n\n*AC28: Editorial link hidden when unpublished*\n\n* Given an editorial link is unpublished or not configured in Contentful for the active storefront, when the mega menu renders, then the corresponding editorial link does not appear.\n\n+*Editorial Image*+\n\n*AC29: Editorial image driven by Contentful*\n\n* Given the mega menu renders for a nav item, when the right panel loads, then the editorial image is fetched from Contentful for that nav item using the active storefront's locale and is not hardcoded in the component.\n\n*AC30: Editorial image fallback*\n\n* Given Contentful content has not been authored or a fetch fails, when the right panel attempts to render, then the editorial image slot does not render and the mega menu remains functional with sub-category links only.\n\n+*Accessibility*+\n\n*AC31: Keyboard and screen reader operability*\n\n* Given a keyboard-only user is interacting with the mega menu, when they navigate and dismiss it, then all interactions are achievable without a mouse and focus is managed correctly throughout.\n\n*AC32: Screen reader state announcement*\n\n* Given a screen reader user is interacting with the mega menu, when they navigate it, then the open/closed state and all links are correctly announced.\n\n*AC33: Reduced motion*\n\n* Given a user has enabled reduced motion at OS level, when the mega menu opens or closes, then any animation respects the reduced motion preference."
  }
}"}

